From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Sheludko <ishell@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:08:08 +0100
Subject: [objects] Disallow JSObject modifications during GC and GC callbacks

Prevent re-entrant modifications to Map transitions, descriptors, and
JSObject shapes from GC callbacks, weak handle callbacks, and Oilpan
sweeping/finalizers, which can corrupt in-progress map and descriptor
updates when triggered mid-operation.

Bug: 577366752

TAG=agy
CONV=4430a477-e227-4e18-b858-0966ccdab79f

Change-Id: I4f770e4dbe7c39d94f19ffa24a2fd2c15f616fb6
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8747642
Commit-Queue: Igor Sheludko <ishell@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Michael Lippautz <mlippautz@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111759}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): cpp-heap.cc: this branch has no WeakProcessingForGlobalHandlesScope block in FinishMarkingAndProcessWeakness, so the two new DCHECKs are added inside a bare `if (isolate_)`; CompactAndSweep() on this branch does not wrap ExecutePreFinalizers() in SweepingOnMutatorThreadForGlobalHandlesScope (upstream 8324ee42ece is not here), so the DisallowJavascriptExecution / DisallowJSObjectModification guards the fix folds into that scope are applied directly around ExecutePreFinalizers(). map.cc: the CHECK is added to ReplaceDescriptors keeping this branch's existing early-return condition.

